# ============================================================================
# Mountie: everything you might want to open as a drive, in one place.
#
#   SSH        a folder on a server: a drive letter on Windows (WinFsp, or
#              Windows' own WebDAV client), a folder in Files on Linux and
#              macOS (sshfs), the Files app on Android. Password, key or the
#              SSH agent; the server's key remembered; Act as root or
#              www-data through sudo.
#   ISO        disk images: ISO, IMG, DMG.
#   VHD        virtual disks: VHD, VHDX (and VMDK, QCOW2, VDI on Linux).
#   Disks      the computer's own disks and sticks, mounted and unmounted.
#   Folders    a folder of yours seen through an ignore list: ~/Downloads as
#              DownloadFiles, showing just the PDFs, say. A real drive, so
#              every app's Open box sees it that way too.
#   RAM        a RAM disk, of the size you say; can keep what's on it.
#   Phone      phones sharing themselves on the Wi-Fi, added as drives; on a
#              phone, Share this phone: its storage as a drive on your computers.
#
#   Lives in the tray, mounts what you ask by itself, can start with the
#   computer. Everything is kept on this device only.
# ============================================================================

@Window Mountie
Title=Mountie
Version=1.3.1
TitleBar=Own
BorderBrush=#127A68
Width=480
Height=700
Icon=mountie.png
AppBar=true
Terms=https://tiny-web.uk/terms.php
UpdateFrom=github:wallisoft/mountie-releases
About=Everything you might open as a drive, in one place: folders on your SSH servers, disk images (ISO, IMG, VHD, VHDX), the computer's own partitions, your folders through an ignore list, and RAM disks. A drive letter on Windows, a folder in Files on Linux and macOS, the Files app on Android. Your passwords and keys stay on this device. Made by Steve (Wallisoft) and Claude, in Visualised.
OnOpened=Start
OnClosing=Closing
AndroidPackage=io.visualised.made.mountie.k7b1ce6cd
AndroidKey=7b1ce6cd

